{
  "version": "schemaxis.readiness/1",
  "routes": {
    "schemaxis.imagej/1": {
      "guide": "docs/imagej.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Threshold one calibrated 8/16-bit grayscale image with headless ImageJ 1.54 and publish verified per-particle measurements (pixel count, area, centroid, bounding box and raw intensity mean/min/max) in declared physical units, ready for Calc or a later R analysis.",
        "assumptions": "ImageJ 1.54 ij.jar (latest release 1.54t qualified) run by a Java 11+ runtime with the jdk.compiler module; a fixed Java source program uses public ImageJ classes headlessly with isolated preferences. Declared pixel width/height and unit replace any calibration stored in the file. Thresholds are inclusive raw stored intensities.",
        "constraints": "One .pgm (P5, maxval 255 or 65535) or uncompressed single-IFD BlackIsZero 8/16-bit unsigned .tif/.tiff, at most 2048 px per side, 1048576 px and 16 MiB; no colour, stacks, ROI, density calibration or inverted LUT. Manual inclusive threshold only; full-range thresholds are rejected. Eight or four connectivity; four requires includeHoles. Size filter is converted to inclusive whole-pixel counts. At least one and at most 4096 particles. Units nm, um, mm, cm or m; pixel size 1e-6..1e6 per side. No arbitrary macros, scripts, plugins or Fiji launcher.",
        "inspection": "particles.csv has one row per particle in ImageJ raster order with unit-bearing column names. particle-summary.json retains image digest/format/bit depth, calibration and coordinate convention, threshold, connectivity, filters, rejected counts, totals and area fraction. count-mask.pgm, native tables and readbacks remain as evidence.",
        "recovery": "INVALID_THRESHOLD: order the bounds and stay within the image bit depth; do not select every pixel. UNSUPPORTED_OPTION: four connectivity needs includeHoles true. INVALID_SIZE_FILTER: widen the area window to contain a whole pixel count. NO_PARTICLES: inspect thresholdPixels and rejected counts, then adjust threshold or filters. INVALID_IMAGE/UNSUPPORTED_IMAGE: convert to a supported plain grayscale PGM/TIFF. INTERPRETER_NOT_FOUND: configure Java (imagej) and ij.jar (imagejJar). UNSUPPORTED_RUNTIME: use ImageJ 1.54 and Java 11+. VERIFICATION_FAILED: keep the run directory and start a fresh attempt."
      },
      "examples": [
